From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 23:39:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: convert fixed-panel HDR signals through calibrated
 DSPP color blocks

The fixed-panel DSPP conversion does not change DSI link timings.
For an SDR colorspace change on an already active fixed panel, keep the
assigned mixers and program their color tables in the same atomic commit.
REGDMA completes before both DSPP flushes are staged. Preserve modesets
for HDR transitions, routing changes and actual mode changes.

Link: https://github.com/MiCode/vendor_opensource_display-drivers/blob/aa06fd1757c28dce96fbe4e04d4530ec21b52aac/msm/sde/sde_encoder.c#L5376

Retry programming both DSPPs on the next active commit when a prior REGDMA transaction fails.

Check the calibrated DSPP layout and colorspace property before enabling output conversion. Compositors can explicitly request a linear gamma ramp without changing the calibrated output. Validate new or modified ramps and reuse immutable ramps on page flips.


Link: https://github.com/slwyts/Project-SunUEFI/commit/f4911b974882b2b09b0000ac05f1b911504c6b05
Link: https://github.com/slwyts/Project-SunUEFI/commit/dcb92e0a1cb9d4fbeffa486eafd79dd6982f9d14
Link: https://github.com/slwyts/Project-SunUEFI/commit/8225035cb676ae83298c7638861ecb23bba7fedb
Link: https://github.com/slwyts/Project-SunUEFI/commit/b71f783f04c0fbdb8ab94e921e20cfcf170f083e
Link: https://github.com/slwyts/Project-SunUEFI/commit/24e9d51c46e4e38cf28a587998281b61f8e5ba9e
Signed-off-by: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
Co-developed-by: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia@gmail.com>
